              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "LIZCANCOOK"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I was missing the tomatoes but otherwise made the recipe as written. Delicious. I was surprised to find this tasted very similar to the dipping sauce the now-closed Thai restaurant by my parents house use to serve with their satay (with more sauce and less veggies). I can't wait to share the recipe with them!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Neil Charles"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I add a piece of ginger and clove crush garlic to the rice vinegar and sugar,then put on low heat to melt sugar, strain and let cool then add pepper flakes,pour over cucumber and red onions,cover and put in refridgerator,sprinkle with peanuts and cilantro when ready to serve.",
            "datePublished": "2017-01-10T16:37:09.210Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "ceewhycee"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was a delicious base for me. I omitted the mint and nuts as I didn't have any on hand and made following adjustments to suit my tastes: adjusted for one serving, used more vinegar (rice) than sugar, used sriracha instead of pepper flakes, and added a little fish sauce. Served with ginger salmon so I tossed in a bag of salad mix for a refreshing salad. Will make again, thank you! May use the dressing for a cold noodle salad dressing as well!",
            "datePublished": "2014-09-13T07:01:46.837Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Tricia"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was so good, perhaps our favorite cucumber salad yet. The red pepper flakes add an unexpected zing. I used toasted cashews instead of peanuts as I didn’t have those; other than slightly over-toasting them (oops) they were a good substitute. Everything else was per the recipe, and I don’t think I’d make any adjustments the next time I make it.",
            "datePublished": "2020-01-11T13:57:25.583Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Stephen"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Use rice vinegar rather than the white stuff - flavor is more complex as well as more subtle. Instead of coriander, use cumin for a deeper tone and a bit of heat. Walla Walla onions make for a more gentle flavor than red onions. 1/3 cup is too much sugar. Sweet mirin is a better choice for a delicate asian flavor.",
            "datePublished": "2014-08-09T15:07:34.537Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "sheenan1"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I only used 2/3 of the amount of sugar this recipe called for and it was still too sweet. Concept is good ... just use less sugar.",
            "datePublished": "2014-01-22T17:47:38.397Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jes"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Amazing! I used 2 medium cucumbers, substituted a yellow onion, one serrano pepper, added 1/2 a sweet orange pepper, 1/2 cup of fresh chopped cilantro, and 2 T sugar. Absolutely incredible flavor that became more and more delicious each day. My only warning: if you don't like the taste of rice vinegar or ginger, stay far away from this recipe.",
            "datePublished": "2009-09-16T14:32:12.580Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "hook214"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Wonderful recipe! I used agave nectar in lieu of sugar and tamari in lieu of salt. Really great! Thanks for sharing!!",
            "datePublished": "2012-02-01T18:19:21.347Z"
          },
          {
